From c07ed9c7cf041ddb2662c9247829f58aba380bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:19:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] runbook 4.1: warn that `series regen` is
 destructive-then-abort, and require a pre-landing baseline

Measured during the lane-209 rank-3 canonical integration, 2026-09-04. `series regen` deletes
every file under patches/series/ BEFORE it runs the linearity pre-flight, so on a branch that
fails that pre-flight - which arifi/main does today, with 10 merge commits - it exits rc=2 having
left the repository with no series at all. 415 tracked .patch files were deleted by what was
intended as a read-only baseline probe; 'git restore -- patches/series/' recovered all of them and
nothing was staged or committed, but an operator who does not know this will read the empty
directory as damage.

Also records the two consequences that cost real time in that lane: nothing new can enter the
public series while merges != 0 (so a fully gated, landed commit can still be absent from
patches/series/, and must then be verified with format-patch + apply --check against the replay
result rather than by hand-editing the series), and the series/provenance/replay baseline must be
taken BEFORE landing, because afterwards a pre-existing failure and a self-caused one are
indistinguishable.

Docs only; no code, no behaviour change.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: none (documentation)
Lane: lane-209
---
 UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md b/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
index 4fa864f2f..2ab392126 100644
--- a/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
+++ b/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
@@ -215,6 +215,30 @@ python tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py provenance        # trailer coverage over
 git rev-list --merges --count <base-sha>..arifi/main    # MUST be 0
 ```
 
+**`series regen` is DESTRUCTIVE-THEN-ABORT. Read this before you run it as a "probe".** It DELETES
+everything under `patches/series/` *first* and only then runs the linearity pre-flight. So on a
+branch that fails that pre-flight — which `arifi/main` does today, with 10 merge commits — it exits
+rc=2 **having left the repository with no series at all**. Measured 2026-09-04 (lane-209 rank 3):
+415 tracked `.patch` files deleted, nothing staged, nothing committed.
+
+Recovery is one command, and the files are tracked so nothing is lost:
+
+```bash
+git restore -- patches/series/          # then confirm: git status --porcelain is EMPTY
+```
+
+Two consequences worth carrying:
+
+- **Nothing new can enter the public series while `merges != 0`.** A commit can be fully gated,
+  landed on `arifi/main`, and still absent from `patches/series/`, because the only lawful way in is
+  a regen that refuses to finish. When that happens, verify the commit at the right scope instead of
+  hand-editing the series (never hand-edit it): `git format-patch -1 <sha>` and `git apply --check`
+  against the result of `series replay --onto <base-sha>`.
+- **Take the baseline BEFORE you land anything.** Run `series check` / `provenance` / `replay` on
+  `arifi/main` first and bank the output. Without that, a pre-existing failure and one your change
+  caused are indistinguishable afterwards, and the honest answer becomes unavailable rather than
+  merely inconvenient.
+
